{
  "base_commit": "1f241bbe2a0a83055af9e744eb3813deab000202",
  "scope": "Hanachan shared Wiggler storage, native lifecycle array access, segment motion names and scalar two-coordinate helper interfaces.",
  "changes": [
    "Replace the scene byte array with fifteen shared Wiggler records and type mTarget accordingly. Share Point with the scene implementation, remove the duplicated full struct C layout, and name the encoded callback words.",
    "Use mWiggler and each record's seg array directly in existing manual constructor/destructor calls. Keep the lifecycle ABI and special callback-copy views; add Point and Wiggler size assertions.",
    "Clarify segment offsets, target angles, bend excess, position outputs, spacing and boundary response. Format the edited movement helpers consistently without changing declaration order, rounding or control flow.",
    "Correct func_0203d5dc from a misleading private Vector3 declaration to two scalar coordinate pairs. Match Hanachan's addition/subtraction declarations to the actual int-pointer definitions and cast at the scalar ABI boundary. This removes eight declaration disagreements without changing the baseline."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "layout": "The existing full local struct C describes a 0x98 record with three callback word pairs, five 8-byte points at+0x18, speed/stretch and animation state. The shared record preserves all fields, offsets and widths. Callback dispatch explicitly reads functionOrOffset and shifts adjustmentAndVirtualFlag right by one, testing bit0 for virtual dispatch. Point size8, Wiggler size0x98 and scene size0x4f68 assert under the pinned compiler.",
    "lifecycle": "The factory constructs fifteen0x98 records at+0x4678; each constructor constructs five8-byte points at+0x18. Destructors clean up those same arrays. Records remain trivial storage and explicit callbacks remain. Both complete objects prove no implicit lifecycle output or relocation change.",
    "geometry": "The segment helpers form relative positions, constrain angle differences to +/-0x2000, rotate offsets and reconstruct segment positions. The boundary helper clamps the movement point and returns bits; MoveBounce retains the matched OR expressions and targets the centre on a boundary hit.",
    "distance_interface": "func_0203d5dc reads only words0 and1 of each input and returns sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy). Its previous private Vector3 misleadingly declared a third unused coordinate and reversed x/y labels. Both MCarlo scene callers pass adjacent mX/mY pairs and mTargetX/mTargetY pairs; their unchanged void-pointer declarations and calls remain ABI-compatible. Hanachan now uses const int pointers; Vec2_Sub and func_0203d704 declarations match their int-pointer definitions.",
    "ownership": "Queue22 state11b2f44bfe0a762bd1af304cc3e359aaa0071b94 has no active dScMgHanachan class/file reservations or overlaps across ov006 text0x020ea280..0x020edec0, init0x02130df8..0x02130e9c, ctor0x021335a0..0x021335a4 and bss0x02142018..0x02142044. No reservation covers the scalar helper arm9 0x0203d5dc..0x0203d614. The daHanachan actor reservation is a separate class/overlay and was left untouched.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator run: layout and names follow explicit accesses, callback dispatch, arithmetic and caller layouts. Coined record names do not assert recovered original names.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep Obj/ObjB/Words2/int[2] callback copy views and nonpolymorphic PMF call views; their different copy lowering is documented matching work.",
      "Keep Render/BeginResult split addresses, raw state-update fields, pointer walks and scalar Fix12 ABI calls with documented matching floors.",
      "Preserve the explicit manual factory/base constructor/vtable sequence, distinct function order, pragmas and native/private output manifests.",
      "Other source declarations of the distance helper remain void pointers. No reserved caller or unrelated shared-header layout was edited."
    ]
  },
